 and administrative decision makers to learn events popularity as quickly as possible, as it can buy extra precious time for them to make informed decisions. Therefore, we introduce the problem of predicting future popularity trend of events on microblogging platforms. Traditionally, trend prediction has been performed by using time series analysis of past popularity to forecast the future popularity changes.","topics":[],"score":2788,"global_rank":33514},{"name":"sayedihashimi/css-layout-samples","owner":"sayedihashimi","html_url":"https://github.com/sayedihashimi/css-layout-samples","stars":1,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"HTML","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2788,"global_rank":33546},{"name":"prestonjcrowe/simple-photo-gallery","owner":"prestonjcrowe","html_url":"https://github.com/prestonjcrowe/simple-photo-gallery","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":24,"language":"HTML","description":"simple and easy photo gallery to showcase my pretty pictures","topics":[],"score":2788,"global_rank":33551},{"name":"xslingcn/Lowkey-Academic-Hugo","owner":"xslingcn","html_url":"https://github.com/xslingcn/Lowkey-Academic-Hugo","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"HTML","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2788,"global_rank":33561}]